3.OBJECTIVES

1.	To Develop a Flood Prediction System
–	Build a system that can predict flood risk using data.
2.	To Use Real-World Dataset
–	Use actual flood and rainfall data for better accuracy.
3.	To Apply Machine Learning Technique
–	Use algorithms like Random Forest for prediction
4.	To Improve Prediction Accuracy
–	Ensure this approach gives correct and reliable results.
5.	To Classify Flood Risk Levels
–	Categorize risk into Low, Medium, and High.
6.	To Reduce Manual Effort
–	Automate the prediction process to save time and effort.
7.	To Support Disaster Management– Help authorities take early preventive actions.
8.	To Enable Future Enhancements
–	Allow improvements like real-time data and time series forecasting.
“These objectives guided us throughout the project development.”
